llion units and approximately 341.0 million square feet of rentable space operating under the Extra Space brand. The Company offers customers a wide selection of conveniently located and secure storage units across the country, including boat storage, RV storage, and business storage. It is the largest operator of self-storage properties in the United States. Extra Space Storage Inc. was incorporated in 1977 in Maryland, USA.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph Daniel Margolis J.D. | CEO & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $3.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $402K ranks in the bottom quartile among Real Estate peers, with revenue growing 18%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $154K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Extra Space Storage Inc is a large-cap real estate business with a $35.3B market cap on $3.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +21% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 13% against a 9% cost of capital, a 4-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $1.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 38 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.90\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.5\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 4.3% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.1\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7509118405835769},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.4M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2369800.0},{"text":"Interest-rate sensitivity and tenant-credit risk \u2014 cap rates and refinancing costs move faster than the 10-year leases can absorb.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Remote work structural vacancy \u2014 the post-pandemic shift to hybrid work has permanently impaired demand for urban office space across most markets.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Climate and insurance cost escalation \u2014 rising premiums and coverage withdrawals in flood/fire zones are repricing assets that the market once treated as perpetuities.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 19% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","21 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Real Estate peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Growing faster than most Real Estate peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Real Estate sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Extra Space Storage (EXR) Up 11.5% Since Last Earnings Report: Can It Continue?","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3036005/extra-space-storage-exr-up-11-5-since-last-earnings-report-can-it-continue?cid=CS-ZC-FT-realtime_blog-3036005","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795707011.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Earnings Beat Change The Bull Case For Extra Space Storage (EXR)?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/earnings-beat-change-bull-case-011259843.html","date":"2026-11-26","timestamp":1795655579.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"ETFs Are Buying Extra Space Storage (EXR) on Nov. 23","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/etfs-buying-extra-space-storage-110204240.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795604524.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"4 Self Storage REITs Turn Spare Space Into Steady Passive Income Dividends","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/real-estate/articles/4-self-storage-reits-turn-133306720.html","date":"2026-11-27","timestamp":1795786386.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.422,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Beach Energy (ASX:BPT): How Far Will the ASX 200 Gas Producer Push Into the Taroom Trough?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/stocks/oil-gas/beach-energy-asxbpt-how-far-will-the-asx-200-gas-producer-push-into-the-taroom-trough","date":"20